# ==============================================================================
# Docker build context exclusions (root context: apps/api and the bot worker)
# ==============================================================================
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# Without it, `docker build .` uploaded a 2.6 GB build context on every single
# build: node_modules (1.2 GB), .venv (1.2 GB) and web/node_modules (145 MB).
# A hosted builder spends minutes receiving files before it compiles anything,
# and Railway's build step times out long before that finishes.
#
# The second, quieter problem was worse. `COPY . ./` in Dockerfile.bot and in
# web/Dockerfile copied the host's macOS node_modules *over* the Linux ones
# already installed inside the image. Native binaries compiled for darwin do
# not run on alpine, so the container died in ways that looked like application
# bugs rather than packaging mistakes.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING — .dockerignore IS NOT .gitignore
# ----------------------------------------------------------
# A pattern containing no `/` matches ONLY at the top level. `*.tsbuildinfo`
# therefore ignores `./tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` and silently lets
# `./packages/types/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` through, whereas the identical line in
# .gitignore does match at every depth, because gitignore treats a slash-less
# pattern as matching any path segment.
#
# That difference was not academic. A stale `packages/types/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`
# reached the image, `tsc --build` read it, concluded the package was already up
# to date, and emitted no `dist/`. Every `@oneteam/*` import then failed with
# TS2307 inside the container while passing on the developer's machine.
#
# Anything that must be excluded at depth uses `**/`. Keep it that way.

# Dependencies are installed inside the image, never copied from the host.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.venv
venv

# Secrets must never reach an image layer, even a private one. The platform
# injects these at runtime; the example files are kept so the list of required
# variables stays discoverable.
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.production.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx

# Build output is produced inside the image, never shipped into it.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Not referenced by either image built from this context.
web
mobile
apps/web
ui-audit
ui-design
docs
.github

# Model weights and media.
**/*.pt
**/*.onnx
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.png
**/*.mp4

# Local tooling, editor state and OS noise.
.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
.workbuddy-ai
.claude
.gemini
.codex
.yolo_config
.torchvision_cache
artifacts
datasets/*
!datasets/README.md
**/*.bak
**/*.log
**/*.orig
**/*.rej
